      {
        "id": 233527,
        "name": "der andere Jan",
        "username": "der_andere_Jan",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/der_andere_jan/{size}/1881_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-08-23T08:39:38.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'd say it makes sense for balancing reasons, the way it is.</p>\n<p>It gives some advantage to characters with less-than-maxed dice, as they are slightly better at passively taking out opponents (think \"jackie chan dodges his way through a group&nbsp;fight\")</p>\n<p>Having crazily high defense (i.e. strong&nbsp;dice)&nbsp;AND passively dishing&nbsp;out&nbsp;is a bit overpowered imho.</p>\n<p>We have to keep in mind that this is a game where&nbsp;not every player creates their character for max efficiency, but for a narrative persona they enjoy. The battle scenes still have to work for these.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:09:22.763Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
